  "blockerDetails": [
    "statsmodels OrderedModel provides the required proportional-odds logit likelihood and probabilities but has no native regularized fit path, so slope-only L2 cannot be pinned without a custom optimizer or subclass",
    "mord LogisticAT provides ordered thresholds, class probabilities and slope-only L2, but optimizes an All-Threshold margin surrogate rather than the ordered categorical likelihood and discards the scipy optimizer result",
    "mord fit returns normally even when max_iter is zero and exposes no convergence success, status, message or iteration attribute, so fail-closed convergence cannot be enforced",
    "scikit-learn LogisticRegression is binary or multinomial, not a proportional-odds ordinal model",
    "no audited candidate satisfies every dependency selection criterion; model semantics are not relaxed"
